WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.560
Speaker 1: as we wait to see whether Donald Trump&nbsp;
will be arrested and indicted in New York. We&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:14.700
have new news out of Georgia that there may be&nbsp;
potential racketeering and conspiracy charges&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:20.280
there coming against the failed former&nbsp;
president Donald Trump. This is again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:27.300
the belief about mounting legal troubles without&nbsp;
yet even knowing whether the New York indictment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:33.120
is going to happen. Now, before I get into the&nbsp;
CNN report about what we have learned. I want to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:41.040
remind people that one of the possibilities, if&nbsp;
and when the New York indictment of Trump comes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:46.260
down, which Trump said would be today, certainly&nbsp;
not seeming like it's going to be today, but we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:52.500
will follow it. One of the reactions was it's kind&nbsp;
of a weak charge. It's not the strongest charge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.500 --> 00:01:00.000
that could be made against Trump. And I agreed&nbsp;
with that. And the hope was that we know there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.520
have been prosecutors who, despite having great&nbsp;
evidence against Trump, have been hesitant to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:12.720
the first to indict a sitting or former president&nbsp;
and now a former president. Is it possible that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:20.400
the Stormy Daniels charges will break the levy and&nbsp;
then we will see other indictments come in? That's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:26.220
the hope. And if that's the case, CNN reports that&nbsp;
Georgia prosecutors are considering racketeering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:32.220
and conspiracy charges. And this is all related to&nbsp;
Trump's effort to overturn the results in Georgia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:39.900
in the 2020 election, where, of course, Joe Biden&nbsp;
won because Joe Biden received more votes. CNN&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:48.840
reports Atlanta area prosecutors are considering&nbsp;
racketeering and conspiracy charges. Fulton County&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:54.840
District Attorney Fani Willis could make decisions&nbsp;
on charges this spring. Willis will bring her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.840 --> 00:02:00.780
charging recommendations to the regularly seated&nbsp;
grand juries, each serving two month terms to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:07.140
regular grand juries were seated in March. The&nbsp;
next batch will be sworn in in May. Investigators&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:12.720
have at least three recordings of Trump pressuring&nbsp;
Georgia officials, including a phone call that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:19.140
made to the Georgia House speaker to push for a&nbsp;
special session to overturn Democrat Joe Biden's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:24.540
2020 victory. There's also a recording of&nbsp;
Trump's call to a top investigator with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:30.120
the Georgia secretary of state's office, where&nbsp;
they were looking into quashed allegations of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:35.820
irregularities with signature matching. And then,&nbsp;
of course, Willis kicked off the investigation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:41.160
soon after the infamous January phone call&nbsp;
wherein Trump pressures Brad Raffensperger to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:50.280
find the votes necessary for him to win. This is&nbsp;
the next layer. Media eight also reporting Trump's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:57.180
legal woes go from bad to worse, as CNN reports,&nbsp;
potential RICO charges for pressuring Joe. Georgia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.180 --> 00:03:04.380
election officials. So what do I believe is going&nbsp;
to happen? I have no idea. As I've said for a long&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:10.320
time, I believe indictments are plausible and&nbsp;
prison time is essentially an impossibility for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:16.020
Donald Trump. I've explained why numerous times,&nbsp;
so I won't do it here. This is very serious stuff.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:21.780
There is no doubt that these are potentially very&nbsp;
serious charges. At the same time, many of you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:27.840
like me, have been stuck in this sort of time&nbsp;
loop where we're always close to possible charges,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:34.980
possible charges stemming from this or that&nbsp;
blatant violation of a law that we read about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:41.400
and yet, quote, Nothing happens. On the one hand,&nbsp;
I feel that frustration. I share that frustration.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:46.740
And there is a feeling that this is just never&nbsp;
going to happen. On the other hand, when you speak&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:53.340
to legal experts, they do say these things take&nbsp;
a while. Oftentimes when you look at white collar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.340 --> 00:04:00.240
crimes by non presidents, just by, you know, a CEO&nbsp;
of a tech company or a bank or whatever the case&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:06.240
may be, it can take years to build these cases.&nbsp;
Here. We're talking about a man who was and is now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:12.000
a former sitting president. And so the timeline&nbsp;
is not actually that unusual. It's just that in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:17.520
most cases, we're not following investigations&nbsp;
and we're not aware of possible charges until&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:22.980
much closer to when those charges are announced.&nbsp;
So I am not really taking a position as to whether&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:27.780
I do or don't think any particular indictment or&nbsp;
charge or arrest is going to happen. Trump said he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:32.460
was getting arrested today. It doesn't seem like&nbsp;
it's happening. And now the discussion is about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:38.700
either tomorrow or next week. I don't know. I&nbsp;
remain convinced, convinced that Trump will never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:44.280
see the inside of a prison cell and that the big&nbsp;
picture of that is that at the very worst case,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:54.060
if there were a plea or a guilty verdict and there&nbsp;
were to be confinement allocated or assigned to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:58.620
Trump, it would be served as home confinement.&nbsp;
I think that that is the absolute worst case&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:03.000
scenario. But we're not even at that step yet.&nbsp;
We are now at this step of there are four at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:09.000
least major investigations into Trump. Will any&nbsp;
of them lead to an indictment or an arrest? We&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:13.980
may know within hours. We may know tomorrow.&nbsp;
We may know next week. But the big news from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:18.660
the last 24 hours is whatever happens with&nbsp;
this New York Stormy Daniels hush money case,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:24.780
it is not the end of the line, as Georgia, I have&nbsp;
believed, is the strongest case for a while now.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:29.880
And it seems as though the most serious charges&nbsp;
could indeed come from there. Leave me a comment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:36.360
Let me know at this point in time. In your&nbsp;
heart of hearts, what do you expect is coming?

